{"content":[{"c":["SUPH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Region mentioned in ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.1.1","r":"Deut.1.1","rawR":"Deut.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.1.1","value":"Deut.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Deuteronomy 1:1"},", which was “beyond the Jordan in the wilderness, in the Arabah over against Suph” (",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"; ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," “the Red Sea”). The exact location of Suph is uncertain. It may refer to the region of Suphah (cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Num.21.14","r":"Num.21.14","rawR":"Num.21.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.21.14","value":"Num.21.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 21:14"},"), east of the Jordan River, or perhaps to the Gulf of Aqaba, the northeastern branch of the Red Sea."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Suph","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Deuteronomy 1:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.1.1","rawQueryValue":"Deut.1.1","sourceRefExact":"Deut.1.1"},{"anchorText":"Nm 21:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.21.14","rawQueryValue":"Num.21.14","sourceRefExact":"Num.21.14"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"3a9ce2a397b0b9076f0d36399963ebf53a7d6e749b7ecb71e2544987d85e0c41","sourceItemName":"Suph","sourceItemOrder":579,"sourceMember":"Articles/S.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Suph","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Suph","title":"Suph","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}